1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,911
Something I'd love to talk about now is apartment living and any cultural shocks that you've had coming from maybe a larger place of living to a smaller one.
接下来我很想聊聊公寓生活：从可能更大的住处搬到更小的地方，你经历了哪些文化冲击？

2
00:00:07,921 --> 00:00:11,600
Because apartments here are very small yeah they really are.
因为这里的公寓很小。是啊，真的很小。

3
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:16,000
Um I grew up like half of my life in an apartment and half in a house.
嗯，我成长过程中，大概一半时间住公寓，一半时间住独立住宅。

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,921
And I would say that the apartment was very just because my parents had both grown up in apartments as well so it was like normal for them.
我会说，那套公寓很……因为我父母也都是住公寓长大的，所以对他们来说很正常；原句 very 后的描述不完整。

5
00:00:23,921 --> 00:00:26,961
Um and then the house we had definitely a lot more space.
嗯，后来住独立住宅时，我们的空间确实多得多。

6
00:00:26,961 --> 00:00:31,761
Um I think the biggest culture shock is like never having alone time truly.
嗯，我觉得最大的文化冲击，就是真的几乎没有独处时间。

7
00:00:31,761 --> 00:00:37,841
I live in a one bedroom with my partner so when we're both home there's like nowhere you can just go and be by yourself.
我和伴侣住一居室，所以两个人都在家时，几乎没有地方能让你一个人待着。

8
00:00:37,841 --> 00:00:40,881
Where they're not going to come in the room and disturb you.
没有哪个地方能保证对方不会走进来打扰你。

9
00:00:40,881 --> 00:00:46,710
Um and so I kind of look forward I think both of us look forward to when we do have outings.
嗯，所以我有点期待——我觉得我们两个都期待——其中一方有外出安排的时候。

10
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:52,711
Because we're like oh good I have the place to myself I can just be um so that was definitely a big adjustment.
因为我们会想，太好了，家里只有我，我可以自在待着。嗯，所以那确实需要很大的适应。

11
00:00:52,721 --> 00:00:59,361
Another one is stairs not every single building has an elevator so having to do lots of stairs.
另一个问题是楼梯。不是每栋楼都有电梯，所以经常得爬很多楼梯。

12
00:00:59,361 --> 00:01:04,241
And even when they do have an elevator they can be so small you can't even fit things that you might need in there.
而且就算有电梯，也可能小得连需要搬进去的东西都放不下。

13
00:01:04,241 --> 00:01:07,121
You can fit like two suitcases and not two people yeah no.
大概能放进两个行李箱，却装不下两个人。是啊，确实。

14
00:01:07,121 --> 00:01:11,911
And if if the two suitcases are there you definitely aren't going in with the two suitcases.
而且，要是两个行李箱都在里面，你肯定就没法和它们一起进去。

15
00:01:11,921 --> 00:01:14,871
You send it up and then run up to find it at the end.
你先让行李上去，再跑楼梯到上面去接它。

16
00:01:14,881 --> 00:01:21,351
And one other thing that I think a lot of people would be shocked by even though we have really hot summers in paris there's no air conditioning.
还有一件我觉得很多人会吃惊的事情：巴黎夏天很热，但她们所说的住处没有空调。

17
00:01:21,361 --> 00:01:23,190
Yeah is that something you grew up with.
是啊，这是你从小就习惯的情况吗？

18
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:28,401
It is something I grew up with in northern california because most houses weren't built with air conditioning.
我在北加州长大时就是这样，因为那里的很多房子建造时没有装空调。

19
00:01:28,401 --> 00:01:35,681
And my parents found no use in building one or putting one in because they're used to no air conditioning.
我父母觉得没必要修建或安装，因为他们已经习惯没有空调了。

20
00:01:35,681 --> 00:01:42,921
Um that was more of a shock for me in paris because uh the summers here are a lot hotter than california at least northern california.
嗯，这在巴黎反而更让我吃惊，因为这里的夏天比加州热得多，至少比北加州热得多。

21
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:49,841
Um northern california you get up to I'm celsius maybe 30 35.
嗯，北加州大概会到——按摄氏温度说——三十、三十五度左右。

22
00:01:49,841 --> 00:01:55,681
Um and there's a breeze cuz we're right by the ocean but here it's pretty stagnant heat.
而且那里有微风，因为我们就在海边；但这里的热气感觉不怎么流动。

23
00:01:55,681 --> 00:02:04,070
Even though you're living in these really small apartments obviously you're surrounded by beauty and a bit of a living museum every day like do you appreciate that more or.
虽然住处这么小，但你每天都被美景包围，仿佛住在一座活的博物馆里；你会更珍惜这些吗，还是……？

24
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:09,441
100 I think the idea of not having like a backyard or a terrace isn't as prevalent.
百分之百会。我觉得，没有后院或露台这件事，就不会那么占据自己的心思了。

25
00:02:09,441 --> 00:02:13,041
Because you just have paris outside of your front steps.
因为走出家门，外面就是巴黎。

26
00:02:13,041 --> 00:02:22,640
And um something that I really appreciate is there are laws in paris that are meant to upkeep their buildings so that they are beautiful at all times.
嗯，我很欣赏的一点是，她理解巴黎有要求维护楼宇的法规，好让楼宇一直保持美观。

27
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:29,361
And that's why you'll see scaffolding everywhere also at all times it just kind of moves from space to space.
所以你也总能在各处看到脚手架，它们只是从一个地方挪到另一个地方。

28
00:02:29,361 --> 00:02:36,481
But because they're required to you know clean their buildings and repaint and every day if you own a business you have to clean in front of your sidewalk.
她说，因为楼宇需要清洁、重新粉刷，而且如果你经营商铺，每天都得清扫门前的人行道。

29
00:02:36,481 --> 00:02:39,921
To make sure it's nice for people to come visit.
这样人们来访时，会觉得这里很舒服、很整洁。

30
00:02:39,921 --> 00:02:48,080
So I do really appreciate that they have this like art and love for cleanliness beauty.
所以我确实很欣赏他们这种对整洁、美感的艺术追求和热爱。

31
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:54,881
Um it some people think it's kind of presumptuous to want things to be beautiful.
嗯，有些人觉得，想让一切都美美的，似乎有点自负。

32
00:02:54,881 --> 00:03:02,241
But that's something that I really appreciate about living here is that it is beautiful everywhere I go and there's a reason because people care and they make it happen.
但这正是我喜欢住在这里的一点：无论走到哪里都很美，而且这是有原因的，因为人们在意，也会付诸行动。
